_print_nvidia_egpu_note() {
    cat <<'EOF'

NVIDIA eGPU hotplug configuration:

- The package's module settings may interfere with an internal NVIDIA GPU.
  Override them with /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-open.conf; an empty file disables
  the module blacklists.

- For a Thunderbolt 4/5 enclosure that is not detected automatically, add this
  per-device option to /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-egpu.conf, replacing the BDF with
  the eGPU's PCI address:

      options nvidia NVreg_RegistryDwordsPerDevice="pci=DDDD:BB:DD.F;RmForceExternalGpu=1"

- Module unloading and process termination are independent settings. Both are
  enabled when unset or empty. To disable module unloading while keeping
  process termination enabled, add this line to /etc/nvidia.env:

      NVIDIA_EGPU_UNLOAD_MODULES=0

- To leave running apps alone, add this line to /etc/nvidia.env. Modules may
  remain loaded if an app still uses them:

      NVIDIA_EGPU_KILL_PROCESSES=0

Keep NVIDIA modules out of the initramfs on eGPU-only systems. Include them
only if the system has an internal NVIDIA GPU.
EOF
}

post_install() {
    _print_nvidia_egpu_note
}

post_upgrade() {
    _print_nvidia_egpu_note
}
